From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: athexweb3 <athexweb3@nirapod.org>
Date: Thu, 8 Oct 2026 19:09:38 +0600
Subject: [PATCH] safetylib: initialization of slice copies at unknown offsets
 and of strings

A copy at an unknown slice offset left the initialization of the
destination cells unchanged. They are now uninitialized if a source cell
that the copy may read is not initialized; otherwise, when their offset
is known, they are initialized (e.g. a slice of a global table). A
string written into a slice initialized the cells from offset 0 and kept
their previous values.

(cherry picked from commit 29e384f22e0eaa87a6e4d9563b1fc7bee9dae07c)
